  "description": "Recounts the Mahabharata’s eighteen-day war through Abhimanyu’s death, the falls of Bhishma, Drona and Karna, Duryodhana’s defeat and the night raid that follows. Examines competing vows, deception, retaliation and the erosion of the warriors’ professed rules, including the losses borne by households and unnamed combatants beyond the famous duels.",
